 "answer": "Use **`Settings.chunk_size`**. It sets the chunk size for LlamaIndex's default `SentenceSplitter` and leaves the splitter itself in place:\n\n```python\nfrom llama_index.core import Settings\n\nSettings.chunk_size = 512\nSettings.chunk_overlap = 50  # optional, set alongside if needed\n```\n\nIf you assign a custom `Settings.node_parser`, the `chunk_size` setting no longer controls splitting, so you would need to set the size on that parser directly. I'm working from memory of the API, so check the current LlamaIndex docs if your version behaves differently.",
